## Initial Q&A
### What is the exact statement made by Kamala Harris about President Abraham Lincoln's nomination of a Supreme Court justice that is the subject of the fact-check?
Answer: During the vice presidential debate, Kamala Harris stated: "Abraham Lincoln was up for reelection, and it was 27 days before the election, and a seat became open on the United States Supreme Court... Abraham Lincoln's party was in charge, not only in the White House, but the Senate... But Honest Abe said, it's not the right thing to do. The American people deserve to make the decision about who will be the next president of the United States, and then that person can select who will serve for a lifetime on the highest court of our land."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/13/fact-check-harris-lesson-lincoln-supreme-court-nom-lacks-detail/5943183002/

### Which Supreme Court justice did President Abraham Lincoln nominate that is being referenced in Kamala Harris's statement?
Answer: President Abraham Lincoln nominated Salmon P. Chase to replace Chief Justice Roger B. Taney, as referenced in Kamala Harris's statement.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/13/fact-check-harris-lesson-lincoln-supreme-court-nom-lacks-detail/5943183002/

### When did this nomination by President Lincoln occur, and under what historical and political circumstances?
Answer: The nomination occurred after the 1864 election, when President Lincoln sent Salmon P. Chase's name to the Senate in December 1864; this was not due to principle but for political expediency, as Lincoln had used the vacant seat to secure support during the election and wanted to manage his coalition during the Civil War.

Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/lincoln-1864-supreme-court/

